   - **Life Sciences:** Revenue up 39% to $464 m, margin 13% (including Varian).  
   - **Chemical Analysis:** Revenue up 60% to $381 m, margin 19% (including Varian).  

   All core platforms (LC, LC/MS, genomics, GC/MS, spectroscopy, etc.) delivered double‑digit growth.

4. **Geographic Diversification** – Organic revenue growth was broad‑based: APAC +27% (23% local‑currency), Europe +22% (19% local‑currency), Americas +12%. This reduces reliance on any single region and cushions against localized macro shocks.

5. **Acquisition Integration & Cost Savings** – The company highlighted successful integration of Varian‑related assets and announced three new acquisitions (Lab901, BIOCIUS, A2 Technologies) that expand electrophoresis, mass‑spec, and spectroscopy capabilities. Management reaffirmed confidence in achieving **$100 m** of net cost synergies from the Varian deal.

