Alumina segment: only segment with sequential decrease ATOI from $125M to $35M. Third-party revenue down $775M (8.5% sequential) due to lower alumina prices. LME-linked alumina prices down ~5%, API spot down >9%. Dollar strength 5% vs USD. One-time land sale $30M not recurring. Productivity offset cost increases: $24M productivity vs $11M cost increase.

Looking forward: alumina surplus continues, curtailments of 390k tons in Atlantic region, production down 100k tons in Q2. Maintenance expenses $10M negative Q2, but expect productivity gains continue.

Primary segment: third-party revenue $1.009B down 2.4%; realized prices up 2% sequential, shipments down 4.2% (more internal). ATOI $10M, up from loss $32M Q4. Market net pricing and FX gave $25M improvement.

Overall: earnings improvement, record segment performance, but still negative free cash flow due to pension contributions and working capital usage. Debt ratio moderate 35.6% (slightly up). Cash $1.7B.

Need to assess outlook: alumina pricing pressure, curtailments, maintenance costs, but productivity improvements. Primary segment shows modest improvement. Overall growth in rolled and engineered segments.

