- Cash from operations hit a historic $1.5 bn in Q4, delivering nearly $1 bn of free cash flow and leaving the balance sheet with $1.9 bn of cash and no commercial paper.  
- The company generated $455 m of free cash flow for the full year, an 18% improvement YoY.  

**Strategic Portfolio Transformation**  
- Completed a $3 bn acquisition (TITAL) and integrated Firth Rixson, expanding value‑added aluminum capabilities.  
- Executed multiple divestitures (European rolling mills, Jamalco interest, Mt. Holly stake) and closed Australian rolling mills, sharpening the asset base.  
- The Saudi alumina refinery is now online, adding a new, geographically diversified source of feedstock.  

**Earnings Quality & One‑Time Items**  
- Net income of $268 m is depressed by a $273 m after‑tax restructuring charge (≈80% non‑cash) and higher effective tax (51% Q4, 64% FY) driven by discrete tax items.  
