Rationale:  

**Revenue & Profitability** – Q3 2015 revenue fell 11% YoY to $5.6 bn, reflecting divestitures, pricing pressure and a weaker euro. Even after a 10% boost from aerospace, automotive and alumina growth, the top line is still down. Adjusted EBITDA of $698 m and free cash flow of $420 m are respectable, but net income is only $44 m (adjusted $109 m) and earnings have slipped $261 m versus a year ago. The high effective tax rate (49% vs a 31% operational rate) underscores the impact of one‑off items.

