**Top‑line & earnings** – Revenue is up 16% YoY (despite a 3% sequential dip) and adjusted net income rose to $150 million ($0.80/share). Adjusted EBITDA, while down $143 million sequentially, is still $99 million higher than a year ago, showing underlying profitability is improving.

