analysisWe need to decide BUY/SELL/HOLD based on earnings call. Summarize: Q3 2018 pre-tax profit $688M excl specials, down $485M YoY due to fuel cost increase. Revenue record $11.6B, up 5.4%, unit revenue up 2.6%, 8th straight quarter of unit revenue growth. Fuel cost up 38% per gallon, hurting margins. CFO mentions cost improvements $300M in 2019 via One Airline, revenue initiatives $1B, growth at DFW hub, capex decreasing after big post-merger spend. Capex 2019 ~ $5B, then down to $3B 2020, $2-3B thereafter. They are bullish, see buying opportunity.

