**Revenue & Growth** – Apple posted $5.26 bn of revenue, a 21 % jump versus the prior March quarter, and net income surged 88 % to $770 m (EPS $0.87). Mac shipments grew 36 % YoY and iPod sales rose 24 % YoY, both well ahead of industry averages. Retail sales were up 34 % YoY, and store margins remain healthy.  

**Profitability** – Gross margin expanded to 35.1 %, beating guidance, thanks to a favorable commodity cost environment, better product mix and operating leverage. Operating margin of 18.7 % is robust for a consumer‑electronics company.  

