**2. Core product strength – HUMIRA** – HUMIRA delivered >19 % global operational growth in the quarter, captured ~25 % of the newly‑launched ulcerative colitis (UC) market in Western Europe, and reinforced its #1 position in the GI biologics space. The brand continues to expand into new indications (e.g., HS) and retains market‑share leadership in dermatology and rheumatology despite biosimilar pressure. This “anchor” product underpins near‑term revenue visibility.

**3. Diversified “steady‑grower” portfolio** – Non‑HUMIRA brands (CREON, Synthroid, Zemplar, Synagis, Duodopa) posted durable growth, providing incremental revenue streams that are less vulnerable to biosimilar erosion.

