**2. Revenue and margin pressure** – Total Q4 revenue slipped 2% and vehicle retail revenue fell 9%, only partially offset by stronger F&I, parts‑service and acquisition contributions. Gross margin held at 15.6% thanks to higher‑margin ancillary businesses, but vehicle margins are compressing (light‑vehicle margin down 70 bps, new‑vehicle margin down 20 bps year‑over‑year). Used‑vehicle unit sales dropped 13% as the sub‑prime segment shrank.  

