   - SG&A at **~28% of sales** reflects continued investment in commercial execution, but also a sizable cost base that will need to be managed post‑separation.

5. **Strategic Separation (Abbott/AbbVie)**  
   - The planned split into a diversified medical‑products company (Abbott) and a research‑based pharma company (AbbVie) is on schedule for year‑end.  
   - Management argues the separation will “provide two unique and compelling investment opportunities,” suggesting potential upside if the market values the pure‑play entities higher than the current conglomerate.  
