5. **Regulatory Tailwind** – The new Medicaid IMD exclusion (effective July 2016) will allow adult Medicaid patients to be treated in freestanding psychiatric hospitals. Acadia reports **~90%** of its facilities already have managed‑Medicaid contracts, and occupancy sits at **79‑80%** with ~20% spare capacity—prime conditions to capture incremental volume once the rule takes effect.

6. **Guidance Consistency** – Management reaffirmed FY 2016 adjusted EPS guidance of **$2.81‑$2.86**, a **26‑28%** increase versus 2015, **excluding** any future acquisition‑related costs. The guidance is realistic given the Q1 performance and the imminent Priory integration.

7. **Risk Considerations** –  
