**Guidance & Headwinds** – FY‑2016 adjusted EPS guidance was trimmed to $2.63‑$2.65 (down from prior expectations) because of a weaker USD/GBP rate and delayed cost‑synergy realization from the Priory transaction. The guidance explicitly excludes any 2016 cost synergies, future acquisition impact, or transaction‑related expenses, suggesting the company is being conservative.  

**Risks** –  
