We need to consider Arch Coal Q2 2011 call. Points: acquisition of ICG, $3B financing, $2B credit facility, synergies $100-120M starting 2012. Record revenues and EBITDA despite volume down 3.5% YoY. Strong Appalachian, Western Bit margins tripled. PRB impacted by flooding, lost 1.5M tons, $15M EBITDA, could lose up to $45M for year. Flood risk ongoing. They see domestic export growth, steel utilization high, US coal exports forecast 106M tons. They have growth plan: 15 million tons met coal by 2015, development projects, expansion in thermal, Singapore office.

