2. **Margin expansion** – The 2020 DCS margin target of 8% (≈ 11.5% on a net‑service‑revenue basis) represents a > 210‑bp improvement versus FY 2018 and builds on a 120‑bp gain already realized in FY 2019. The firm is actively pursuing additional upside through shared‑service and global‑design‑center efficiencies, which should further protect margins.

3. **Strategic balance‑sheet de‑risking** – The $2.405 bn sale of the Management Services business (at a premium) will inject a sizable cash windfall. Management plans to use the proceeds to (a) reduce debt, (b) repurchase shares at what they deem a “substantial discount” to intrinsic value, and (c) fund remaining growth initiatives. This should improve leverage metrics and boost EPS.

