Rationale:  

**Revenue & Growth** – Accenture posted record FY‑2016 revenue of $32.9 bn, up 10.5 % in local‑currency terms, and delivered double‑digit growth for a second consecutive year. Q4 revenue of $8.5 bn grew ~9 % in local currency, beating the upper end of its prior guidance after FX headwinds. New bookings of $35.4 bn (7 % LC growth) and a Q4 book‑to‑bill >1.0 underscore a healthy pipeline.

