Rationale:  

**Earnings & Margins** – Q2 2012 net earnings collapsed to $80 million ($0.12 EPS) versus $1.14 billion a year earlier, an 89 % decline. Even on an adjusted basis, EPS fell from $1.20 to $0.51. Segment operating profit (excluding the PHA impairment) dropped from $1.4 billion to $648 million. The weakness stems from lower oilseed margins, soft corn results and poor international merchandising.  

