analysisWe need to analyze the earnings-call statement and decide BUY/HOLD/SELL. The transcript is garbled, with many filler, unclear statements, but we can extract some points: Q2 2009 earnings per share $0.68 (non-GAAP?), annual ongoing earnings $1.55 per share. Rate adjustments $2.7B over years. O&M under budget $100M. Guidance $2.75-$3.05 (presumably EPS?). Some issues: Ohio ESP rehearing order disappointment, Ormat cash to deferred collection, plant acquisitions (Waterfront Derby plant, Peaker Darby) with concerns. Legal/regulatory issues in Arkansas. Building Turk Station (ultra supercritical coal). Federal legislation (Waxman-Markey) discussion, but seems supportive. Overall tone is somewhat rambling, some positive points but also many uncertainties, legal/regulatory headwinds, unclear guidance.

