2. **Asset‑sale “de‑risking” ahead of plan** – The company has completed **$540 million** of asset sales this year, more than double the $200‑$300 million range originally set. This not only shrinks the balance sheet but also provides a sizable cash cushion.  

3. **Capital‑allocation discipline** – $300 million of debt was prepaid (exceeding the $200 million full‑year goal), improving credit metrics and reducing financing risk.  

4. **Construction progress on‑time and on‑budget** – **2.4 GW** of capacity under construction has been brought online as scheduled, and the overall construction program (3.9 GW, $7.8 bn capex) is being funded largely through non‑recourse financing, limiting equity exposure to roughly **$1.3 bn**.  

