1. **Earnings Trend** – Core net operating earnings fell 21% YoY to $103 M ($0.91/share). While net earnings per share rose 6% (thanks largely to a $3 M share‑repurchase program), the underlying operating performance is weakening, driven by lower P&C underwriting profit, weaker investment income, and higher borrowing costs from the 2009 $350 M debt issuance.  

