**1. Earnings momentum** – Core net operating earnings per share rose 5% YoY to $1.35, setting a new record for both the quarter and the full year. Underwriting profit in the Specialty Property & Casualty segment increased (Q4 $79 m vs $75 m a year earlier) and the combined ratio stayed comfortably below 100 % (92.6%).  

**2. Capital returns to shareholders** – Management paid a $169 m dividend package, including a $88 m special dividend, and raised the regular dividend by 14% to a $1 annual rate. In addition, $191 m of common stock was repurchased at an average price of $57.73, indicating confidence that the stock is undervalued relative to intrinsic value.  

**3. Strong total‑shareholder performance** – Over the past five years, adjusted book‑value per share (plus dividends) grew at a 12% compound rate, while total shareholder return (price appreciation + dividends) averaged 23% per year—well ahead of the S&P 500 and the S&P Property & Casualty indices.  

