**Guidance and outlook** – Management projects 2017 core earnings of $6.20‑$6.70 per share, implying a 3‑plus‑fold increase from the Q4 level, consistent with the historical growth trajectory. The guidance assumes the current 35% corporate tax rate, but management acknowledges potential reform risk while remaining optimistic about a “rebirth” of the reinsurance sector.

**Segment resilience** – Property & transportation underwriting showed double‑digit profit improvement, driven by strong crop insurance and inland‑marine results. Workers‑comp profitability was also highlighted. While specialty casualty underwriting was weaker (NY contractor losses, higher excess‑line losses), the company identified the issue and indicated corrective pricing/underwriting actions.

