- **Margin pressure:** Pretax earnings fell 1.4% in the quarter (down to JPY 78 bn) despite the sales surge, reflecting lower assumed interest rates on the WAYS and child‑endowment products. The company is already cutting the discounted‑advance‑premium (DAP) credit, which will further squeeze short‑term profitability.  
