We need to consider Aflac Q3 2019 call. Points: strong earnings, capital, pretax margins stable, robust capital, high ROIC, low cost of capital. Revised 2019 adjusted EPS outlook upward. However challenges: Japan sales decline, especially cancer insurance down 37.7% YoY, Japan Post channel decline possibly 50% drop. Overall Japan earnings down mid-teens, earned premium growth only 1%. US sales flat to down slightly, growth in earned premium 2% expected. Macro headwinds: labor market reduces independent agents, partnership review disruption. But positive: medical insurance sales up 24.5% YoY, direct-to-consumer platform, broker strategies, acquisition of Argus Dental & Vision to drive growth. Dividend growth 37 years.

Overall, the company shows strong financial strength, but growth is modest, with some headwinds especially in Japan. However management is confident about 2020 recovery, acquisition to boost growth, and dividend track record.

