Rationale:  

- **Operating performance:** The company posted $136 million of operating income ($0.73 EPS), which is solid on a quarterly basis. New municipal origination volume jumped 32 % QoQ, indicating healthy pipeline growth.  

- **Loss development:** Reported economic loss development of $71 million was driven almost entirely by a $60 million GAAP discount‑rate charge rather than actual credit deterioration. The underlying credit performance appears sound – municipal defaults are well below 2009‑10 levels and there have been no material defaults in the insured portfolio.  

