analysisWe need to analyze earnings call statement for Assured Guaranty (AGC) Q1 2013. Determine BUY/HOLD/SELL. Provide decision numeric: 0 for Buy, 1 for Sell, 2 for Hold.

We need to consider operating income up 266% YoY, cash payment from UBS $358M, loss-sharing arrangement, reduction of liability on 55% of remaining par, share repurchase $115M, termination of policies $1.6B, new business down (PVP $18M vs $34M prior year), but still some production. Concerns: Moody's rating action causing dislocation, low interest rates, tight spreads, limited new business, reliance on capital management. Overall positive operating performance, capital strength, but growth limited, rating risk.

